# Line endings are pinned here, not left to the machine.
#
# core.autocrlf is enabled system-wide on the Windows workstation this repo is
# developed on, and there was no .gitattributes, so every commit printed "LF
# will be replaced by CRLF" and a fresh clone checked text files out with CRLF
# while CI (ubuntu) checked the same bytes out with LF. Verified by cloning to
# a temporary directory: `git ls-files --eol` reported `i/lf w/crlf` there,
# against `w/lf` in this older checkout, which merely predates the change.
#
# It mattered first for a generated SCSS file compared byte for byte, removed
# by ruling R38 once it had no consumer. It still matters, and for the same
# reason: FW7 compares generated SVG strings byte for byte across Node and the
# browser, and commits Playwright screenshot baselines. An EOL that varies by
# machine breaks a byte comparison in one direction and hides a real drift in
# the other, and the reflexive fix - normalising before comparing - blinds the
# check to exactly the EOL-only and trailing-newline-only edits it exists to
# catch. Pinning LF keeps every such comparison exact.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces: text=auto already detects these as binary, but naming them
# means a corrupted heuristic cannot mangle an image.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pmtiles binary
